{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHosLDm8fZJdnddXo47","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 10 (Sb fraction 0.26) as the best composition, but no composition on this Mg–Sb–O line showed a real photoresponse. Its EQE of 0.00024% is the highest reading only on paper and isn't meaningfully above the others.\n\nI used all 5 EQE measurements, spread across the line so any active region would show up:\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.09 | 0.00011 |\n| **10** | **0.26** | **0.00024** |\n| 16 | 0.45 | 0.0 |\n| 22 | 0.67 (MgSb₂O₆ composition) | −0.00063 |\n| 27 | 0.80 | −0.00057 |\n\nEvery value is within about ±0.0006% of zero, which is measurement noise. That's what I expected going in: the known phases in this system (MgO, MgSb₂O₆ and the antimony oxides) have wide band gaps, so they should absorb almost none of the 2.4 eV light.\n\nI didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements. The remaining 24 compositions are unmeasured, so a small active region between my sample points can't be ruled out, though these phases give little reason to expect one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":511,"cache_read_input_tokens":7396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":511},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67313784-071b-4e08-96ca-8c25677386ea","uuid":"15450d13-e14d-4707-9c7a-32c9626854e2","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:41:15.574Z","request_id":"req_011CfAHorsvkwNwJN3A9Gfh1"}
